<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    GH-558 (secondary complaint, and what the PHADE dataset repro keys on):
    standalone pointer arithmetic is rendered as `p->r + i` instead of array
    notation, because PrintC::opPtradd only uses subscript form inside a
    load/store context.

    Bytes: the `foo` function from the issue's own attached binary (foo.zip,
    gcc 13.3 -O3, x86-64), at its original address 0x1120:

        typedef struct { unsigned int n; unsigned int **r; } S;
        extern void init(unsigned int *x);
        void foo(S *p) {
            for (int i = 0; i < p->n; i++)
                init(p->r[i]);
        }

    Default output renders the PTRADD as `p->r + lVar` (pointer-arith form).

    Stage model: which notation a standalone PTRADD gets is an S9
    "literal/format policy" decision (LATENT upstream).  kuna exposes it as the
    P0 assertion `option arraynotation on|off`; when on, PrintC::opPtradd emits
    `&base[index]` instead of `base + index`.

    Pass 1 (default) proves the issue reproduces; pass 2 (option on) proves the
    stage-level intervention fixes the rendering.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1050" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1120" readonly="true">
f30f1efa8b0785c0742e554889fd5331db4883ec080f1f00488b4508488b3cd84883c301e807ffffff3b5d0072ea4883c4085b5dc30f1f00c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1050" name="init"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1120" name="foo"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line struct S { uint4 n; uint4 **r; };</com>
  <com>parse line extern void init(uint4 *x);</com>
  <com>parse line extern void foo(S *p);</com>
  <com>lo fu foo</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option arraynotation off</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH558 #3: arraynotation off restores upstream pointer arithmetic (old behavior, opt-in)" min="1" max="1">= p-&gt;r \+ </stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH558 #4: default pipeline renders &amp;p-&gt;r[i] (fix is DIV-2 default)" min="1" max="1">= &amp;p-&gt;r\[</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
